const executionReqs = "The certification of trust must be in the form of an affidavit signed and acknowledged by ALL of the currently acting trustees (Idaho Code § 68-114(2)). This is stricter than UTC states, which require only one trustee to sign. 'Acknowledged' means notarized acknowledgment. No witnesses or recording are specifically required for the certification. Idaho's certification of trust provisions predate the UTC (added 1998, ch. 302).";
